    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. The workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now being created when running `frai gate init --ci`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Bug:** The `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. The `--ci` flag was being consumed by Commander.js's option parsing at the parent command level and not being passed through to the `frai-gate` subprocess.\n\n**The Fix:** I modified the `gate` command handler in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d10/without/t1-flag-bug/r2/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to pass all original process arguments directly to the spawned `frai-gate` CLI, bypassing Commander's argument parsing. \n\nChanged from:\n```typescript\n.action(async (args: string[]) => {\n  // ...\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...(args ?? [])], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nTo:\n```typescript\n.action(async () => {\n  // ...\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...process.argv.slice(3)], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nThis ensures all flags like `--ci`, `--smart`, and `--json` are correctly forwarded to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**Verification:** The package was rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested successfully\u2014running `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.",
